# The terminator conformance fixture's retired server key. A PEM file tolerates
# explanatory text before the encapsulation boundary (RFC 7468 section 5.2), so
# the marker fits on the line above the delimiter. RFC 7468 s2 permits text before
# the encapsulation boundary, so a REAL key with this comment above it still parses
# -- confirmed with `openssl pkey -noout` on a generated 2048-bit key. THIS file does
# not, and cannot: its payload is placeholder base64 that decodes to English, because
# a fixture carrying a parseable private key would be the thing the gate forbids.
# not-a-live-credential: key pair retired at the terminator on 2026-03-14, kept because the handshake refusal case needs a real PEM to reject
-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
bm90YXJlYWxrZXl0aGlzaXNhZml4dHVyZXBheWxvYWRkb25vdHVzZWl0YW55d2hl
cmVpdGlzc2l4dHlmb3VyY2hhcmFjdGVyc29mcGxhY2Vob2xkZXJiYXNlNjRvbmx5
-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
